{
  "review": "From the very beginning, the political theme of this film is so obvious and heavy handed that the outcome is entirely predictable. Any good textbook on writing screenplays will advise layering of characters, incorporating character arcs, and three act structure. In this film you will find none of that. The police are the baddies, and consequently are shown as shallow, incompetent and cowards. It never seems to occur to the makers of this film that police might be honourable citizens who see joining the police as a good way to contribute to the wellbeing of society.",
  "translate": "Dal very inizio, il tema politico di questo film è così ovvio e accattivante che il risultato è interamente previsto. Qualsiasi buon libro sulla scrittura dello script consiglia la sovrapposizione degli argomenti, l'arco delle personaggi e la struttura tridimensionale. In questo film troviamo nessuno di questi. I poliziotti sono i badi, e di conseguenza vengono mostrati come ingnightili, inconvenienti e cattivi. Non sembra che i makers di questo film considerino che i poliziotti possano essere Ciudadini onori che si verghino per contribuire alla benavolta della società.",
  "sentiment": "negative",
  "emotion": "disgust"
}

{
  "review": "I think the problem with some reactions to this film is that - with few exceptions - they don't focus on the main disconnect, hence the main split in the audience.<br /><br />On one side, there are those who are taken by the visual design, pretty costumes, and variety of elements going into the film. Some children's movie fans love the colour and animation, and all the un-scary 'magical' effects, shapeshifting animals, and so on. Some culture vultures like the complicated references, the layerings of different folklore elements, and the fact that they can watch Zhang Ziyi singing and quasi-miming, in two different languages, in what really was intended to be a children's comedy.<br /><br />On the other side, there are those who say that a children's movie should still have a point, that a blend of folktales is not a tale at all, and that it's easier to believe in magic when enough thought and care has gone into the technical aspects to make it seem real.<br /><br />In other words, the ideas could be lovely; but when you put them onstage they have to deliver. Here, they don't.<br /><br />A good folktale - from any country - has a clear story, a point, and characters who interact strongly with each other. This lacks them all. A few over-sophisticated gestures to opera, Western and Japanese, are no replacement for a solid theme.<br /><br />As a fantasy fan, I must say that I've sat through some turkeys and loved a few, but this one really tries to do too many things - cheaply. Putting in Zhang Ziyi to try to add a little glitter smacks of exotic flower syndrome. The other problem isn't that there's no plot; there's half a plot, which means that you keep getting pulled in, then dropped again as another none-too-sharply-executed dance number kicks off.<br /><br />The characters all seem to know that they're starring in a movie. Unless you really like watching other peoples' amateur video, this ain't good. I'd like to test this on real children; I think they'd drop it for Uproar in Heaven after about 20 minutes.",
  "translate": "Lo siento di que algunos reacciones a este film no se centran en la des-connectividad principal, lo que causó el split principal en el público.<br /><br />Por un lado, hay aquellas personas que son taknadas por la diseño visual, los costos bellicosos y los elementos variados que entran al film. Algunos fanos de películas para menores disfrutan de la coloración y animación, así como de todos los efectos mágicos incansables, los bestias que se transforman, etc. Algunos defensores de la cultura apretan las referencias complejas, las superposiciones de elementos folklore y la idea de ver Zhang Ziyi cantar y monear en dos idiomas diferentes, lo cual se supone que es una comedia infantil.</br><br />Por otro lado, hay aqellas personas que dicen que una película para menores debería tener un punto, que una mezcla de narrajes no es un testimonio, y que resulta más fácil creer en la mágica cuando se han puesto ogros y esfuerzos técnicos para que parezca real.<br /><br />En efecto, las ideas podrían ser hermosas; pero cuando stalan al teatro deben demostrarse. En este caso, no lo hicieron.<br /><br />Un folktale de buena calidad - de cualquier país -, debe tener una historia clara, un punto y caracteres que se interaccionan fuertemente entre sí. Este carece de todos estos aspectos. Unos pocos gestos super-sophisticados hacia la operación, occidental e japoníces son imposibles de reemplazar por un único thema sólido.</br><br />Como fan de fantasía, di que he assistido a algunas películas y disfruté de algunas, pero esta una tentativa que se hace demasiado de las cosas - de manera barata. Colocar a Zhang Ziyi para añadir una poca brillo trivial. El otro problema no es que no haya un plot; hay mitad de plot, lo cual significa que te mantienes encantado por unos minutos y caes interesting cuando surgen más danced numéricos sin más ejecuciones.</br><br />Los personajes parecen saben que están en un film. A menos que prefieras observar a otros泡沫 video, esta película no es divertida. Me gustaría probar esta película con los niños; creo que dansería por Uproar in Heaven después de unos 20 minutos.",
  "sentiment": "negative",
  "emotion": "disgust"
}

{
  "review": "At first, pensiero che potrebbe essere un comodefghi/psico但仍看到一个女人在浴缸里尖叫不休，这让我有点不安。但随着影片发展，感觉越来越平淡无奇。情节愚蠢，一个男人因为房价上涨而心烦意乱，联系了当地的电台心理医生大骂一通，因为他没更好的选择。然后警方介入，试图让我们感到他们真的关心是谁在打电话，并尽一切努力追踪这个人。一个接一个的嫌疑人被指控。这部电影糟糕极了，缓慢发展的爱 scenes between Adrian B. 和她的丈夫变得无聊，让我只是快进电影。avoid它!",
  "translate": "All'inizio, pensavo che potesse essere un comodefghi/psico, ma vedendo una donna in banca nel bagniTutto sembrava che stessa gridare continuously. Ma al progressive della scena, il film si diventa piu' banale. Un uomo che ha paura di fare altro deciderà di chiamare un psicologo e di grattare le dita perché non ha altro da fare. Poi la legge entra in gioco per tentare di farceli capire chi è il testimone e cerca di trascinare il cazzo fuori. Un'imposto suscita che si nascondono i culi sono accusati. Questo film è banale e le escursioni lento delle amour scenes between Adrian B. E il suo ex marito sono banali, mi portano a salutare la fuga dal film. Evitalo!",
  "sentiment": "negative",
  "emotion": "anger"
}

{
  "review": "When many people say it's the 'worst movie I've ever seen', they tend to say that about virtually any movie they didn't like. However, of the nearly 700 movies I can remember ever seeing this one is one of two that I walked away from feeling personally insulted and angry. This is my first movie review, by the way, and I registered with IMDb just to rave at this movie's badness. I went to see it when it was in the theaters (myself and my two buddies were 3 of 5 people there), and after 15 years I can't remember very many specifics, but my attitude upon leaving the theater is still crystal clear.",
