{
  "review": "Why di you buy this flick on DVD?, Well the snap shot would be: I genuinely don't know. For the extended version, it pretty much boils down to the fact that I actually like Tatyana Ali and she plays Alicia in this.<br /><br />Now does Tatyana Ali give a really good effort in this movie? I must say that it is one of the better, and she is shaping up to be a rather decent actress. I am looking forward to seeing her in action when better material comes available.<br /><br />This being said, this flick was terrible - and my score is based on this: 1 star for not being the worst movie I've seen, 1 star for Tatyana Ali's performance, and 1 star for not thinking that it only deserves 2 stars, there are worse movies out there.<br /><br />Ja Rule should stick to rapping, not my favorite rapper to say the least, but some do like him - and if he is contained there, I would be delighted not to see him tainting the acting scene.<br /><br />Ving Rhames: Ah man, Marcellus Wallace what are you doing here - you used to be cool man. Just because Michael Caine is a really brilliant actor, who has been in so many terrible films as well as good ones, you don't have to copy him Ving.<br /><br />The rest of the semi big names in the cast: It's okay, there are bills to pay, and we all have to do things we're not proud of sometimes.<br /><br />The flick itself. It so massively flawed; it's hard to know where to start. It's more like a bunch of scenes thrown together, as if the director said "we need to tell this, and we need to tell that." There is a story, unfortunately nothing surprising or within it. To be honest, the plot changes in the story were obvious and therefore predictable what was going to happen all the time.<br /><br />In summary: Definitely not good.",
